<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adna Chaffee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1842–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adna Chaffee was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army officer who commanded the American contingent in the relief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> legations during the Boxer Rebellion in 1900. In 1901 he succeeded Arthur MacArthur as military governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, a post that ended in 1902 as civil government took over. He later served as Chief of Staff of the United States Army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adna-chaffee.jpg" alt="Adna Chaffee" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miscellaneous Items in High Demand, PPOC, Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gen._Adna_R._Chaffee,_half-length_portrait,_facing_left,_in_uniform_LCCN97508364_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
